# Development Phases

# Phase 0 — Knowledge Foundation

## Purpose

Create the authoritative knowledge base from which the architecture will be designed.

---

## Inputs

Examples

- Books
- Research Papers
- Enterprise Frameworks
- Standards
- Company Policies
- Internal Procedures
- Regulations
- White Papers
- Subject Matter Expert Interviews

---

## Activities

### Knowledge Acquisition

Collect authoritative knowledge sources.

---

### Knowledge Validation

Validate that sources are:

- authoritative
- current
- complete
- relevant

---

### Knowledge Engineering

Transform raw knowledge into structured knowledge.

```
Books

↓

Concepts

↓

Relationships

↓

Rules

↓

Constraints

↓

Principles

↓

Ontology

↓

Knowledge Objects
```

---

### Knowledge Repository

Store structured knowledge within the Enterprise Knowledge Base.

---

### Knowledge Governance

- Versioning
- Review
- Approval
- Maintenance
- Retirement

---

## Outputs

- Enterprise Knowledge Base
- Knowledge Objects
- Ontology
- Concept Relationships
- Business Rules
- Constraints
- Principles
- Domain Taxonomies
- Knowledge Graph
- Source References

---

## Deliverable

