---

# Development Rules

- Knowledge before Architecture.
- Architecture before Implementation.
- Never skip phases.
- Never implement features without approved architecture.
- Never implement multiple Work Packages simultaneously.
- Every Work Package must be independently testable.
- Every Work Package must pass architectural compliance.
- Every Work Package must be committed before continuing.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless architecture explicitly changes.
- Maintain strict separation of concerns.
- Design loosely coupled and highly cohesive modules.
- Maintain complete traceability from knowledge to implementation.

---

# Success Criteria

A project developed using AFDF is considered successful when:

- Architecture is derived from authoritative knowledge.
- Every architectural decision has a traceable knowledge source.
- Every implementation is traceable to architecture.
- No production code violates architectural decisions.
- Every Work Package is independently testable.
- The platform remains modular, extensible, maintainable, and governed throughout its lifecycle.
